Guard the failure path in the ALSA driver against closing a NULL handle.

ALSA_Init_internal jumps to END: when snd_pcm_open fails, and END:
unconditionally calls snd_pcm_close(pcm_h). snd_pcm_open leaves pcm_h at
its static NULL on failure, and alsa-lib's snd_pcm_close begins with
assert(pcm) — so a machine with no usable "default" PCM does not get
"sound off", it gets

    ALSA lib pcm.c:2722:(snd_pcm_open_noupdate) Unknown PCM default
    Assertion failed: pcm (pcm.c: snd_pcm_close: 779)

and the whole process aborts inside MikMod_Init, past any error check the
caller could make. Every KDOS box without a loaded sound driver hit this.

--- a/drivers/drv_alsa.c
+++ b/drivers/drv_alsa.c
@@ -332,8 +332,10 @@
 		return 0;
 	}
 END:
-	alsa_pcm_close(pcm_h);
-	pcm_h = NULL;
+	if (pcm_h) {
+		alsa_pcm_close(pcm_h);
+		pcm_h = NULL;
+	}
 	return 1;
 }
 
